<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/free-claim-calculators/">Calculators</a></li><li aria-current="page">Appraisal Payoff Calculator</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Free calculator</p><h1>Appraisal Payoff Calculator: Will Appraisal Pay Off for You?</h1><p class="lede">Enter the insurer’s estimate and yours, choose where an award might land, and add realistic fees. The calculator shows whether appraisal is likely to leave you better off.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool" data-tool="gap">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal payoff calculator</span><i>Runs in your browser</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="g-ins">Insurer’s estimate (RCV)</label><input id="g-ins" name="insurer" inputmode="decimal" value="23600"><span class="hint">Replacement cost total on the insurer’s estimate.</span></div>
        <div><label for="g-own">Your estimate (RCV)</label><input id="g-own" name="yours" inputmode="decimal" value="38900"><span class="hint">Your contractor’s or independent estimate.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div><label for="g-land">Where might the award land within the gap?</label>
        <div class="range"><input id="g-land" type="range" name="land" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="55" data-unit="%"><output>55%</output></div>
        <span class="hint">0% means the insurer’s number holds. 100% means your full number is awarded.</span></div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="g-ft">Your appraiser’s fee type</label><select id="g-ft" name="feetype"><option value="flat">Flat fee ($)</option><option value="pct">Percent of increase (%)</option></select></div>
        <div><label for="g-fee">Fee amount</label><input id="g-fee" name="fee" inputmode="decimal" value="3000"></div>
      </div>
      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="useump" checked> Include half of an umpire’s fee</label>
      <div><label for="g-ump">Umpire’s total fee (split 50/50)</label><input id="g-ump" name="umpire" inputmode="decimal" value="3600"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="out-big"><small>Estimated net increase to you</small><b data-o="net">$0</b></div>
      <div class="stack" aria-hidden="true"><span class="s1"></span><span class="s2"></span><span class="s3"></span></div>
      <div class="legend"><span><i class="s1"></i>Insurer’s number</span><span><i class="s2"></i>Your net gain</span><span><i class="s3"></i>Appraisal costs</span></div>
      <div class="out-rows">
        <div><span>Amount in dispute</span><b data-o="gap">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Gap as % of insurer’s estimate</span><b data-o="pct">—</b></div>
        <div><span>Projected award (RCV)</span><b data-o="award">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Gross increase</span><b data-o="gain">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Your appraisal costs</span><b data-o="cost">$0</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="out-msg" data-o="msg"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you enter is stored.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>How to use it</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Enter the insurer’s RCV total</strong>, the replacement cost before depreciation and deductible.</li>
<li><strong>Enter your estimate</strong> from a contractor or independent estimator, also at RCV.</li>
<li><strong>Move the slider</strong> to test outcomes. Try 30%, 50% and 80% to see a range instead of one answer.</li>
<li><strong>Add fees</strong> using your appraiser’s quoted arrangement and a realistic umpire fee.</li></ol>
<h2>Why test a range</h2>
<p>Awards rarely match either side’s opening number. Well-documented items tend to hold and unsupported ones tend to fall. If appraisal only pays off at 90% or 100%, the case is fragile. If it still works at 40%, it’s more likely worth pursuing.</p>
<h2>What it leaves out</h2>
<p>The calculator doesn’t account for depreciation timing, limits or deductibles, which affect what you’re paid but not the size of the dispute. For holdback math, use the <a href="/free-claim-calculators/replacement-cost-holdback-calculator/">replacement cost holdback calculator</a>.</p>
<p class="hint">Example figures loaded in the calculator are illustrative only.</p>
<h2>Questions about this calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is the projected award a guarantee?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. It’s a planning scenario. Real awards depend on documentation, the panel and the policy.</p></div></details><details><summary>What’s a typical umpire fee?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It varies with the size and complexity of the claim. The appraisers can get a quote once an umpire is proposed, and the cost is usually split evenly.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free calculators</h2><div class="cards3 tight"><a class="pcard rv" href="/free-claim-calculators/replacement-cost-holdback-calculator/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/calculator-desk.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/calculator-desk-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/calculator-desk.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Free calculator</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Replacement Cost Holdback Calculator</h3><span class="pcard-p">Estimate your first ACV check, the depreciation held back and the total once repairs are done.</span><span class="pcard-more">Open <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/free-claim-calculators/roof-pitch-squares-calculator/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roof-shingles.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roof-shingles-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roof-shingles.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Free calculator</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Roof Pitch &amp; Squares Calculator</h3><span class="pcard-p">Turn a footprint into true roof squares using pitch and waste, then check the insurer’s figures.</span><span class="pcard-more">Open <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/free-claim-calculators/percentage-deductible-calculator/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/seattle-skyline.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/seattle-skyline-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/seattle-skyline.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Free calculator</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Percentage Deductible Calculator</h3><span class="pcard-p">Turn a percentage earthquake, wind or hail deductible into dollars and see what a claim would pay.</span><span class="pcard-more">Open <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-in"><div class="side-box call-box"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through, free</h2><p>Tell us what happened and what the insurer offered. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits.</p><a class="call-num" href=